From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:07:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: reject cropped or scaled cursor planes

The cursor can't crop or scale: NVKMS always shows the whole surface at its
own size. cursor_plane_req_config_update() only used the framebuffer and
CRTC_X/Y, so a commit with a source rectangle or CRTC size that doesn't match
the framebuffer passed and showed the wrong image. KWin can put client
surfaces on the cursor plane when their size on screen matches a size hint,
even if the buffer is larger. Fail the commit, so that the compositor can fall
back to composition.

KWin's own cursor, aquamarine, wlroots, mutter and the legacy cursor ioctls all
use the whole framebuffer at its own size, so they aren't affected.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 7ca5e044..88099c75 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -318,6 +318,20 @@ cursor_plane_req_config_update(struct drm_plane *plane,
     if (req_config->surface == NULL) {
         return -EINVAL;
     }
+
+    /*
+     * The cursor can't crop or scale: NVKMS always shows the whole surface at
+     * its own size. Fail the commit instead of showing the wrong image, so that
+     * the compositor can fall back to composition.
+     */
+    if (plane_state->src_x != 0 || plane_state->src_y != 0 ||
+        plane_state->src_w != (plane_state->fb->width << 16) ||
+        plane_state->src_h != (plane_state->fb->height << 16) ||
+        plane_state->crtc_w != plane_state->fb->width ||
+        plane_state->crtc_h != plane_state->fb->height) {
+        return -EINVAL;
+    }
+
     req_config->dstX = plane_state->crtc_x;
     req_config->dstY = plane_state->crtc_y;
 
